Q: I am trying to call a constructor with an argument list, but my IDE shows an error: “member […] is not a type name”. How to resolve this? A: <p>Within a class definition, something of the form <code>camera_manager::EmulatorCameraMng m_emulator_manager(m_parser);</code> is syntactically a member function declaration. You get an error there because you name an object not a type.</p>

<p>You will need to pass <code>m_parser</code> to <code>m_emulator_manager</code> in each constructor's member initialiser list, e.g.</p>

<pre><code>class Foo {
    EmulatorCameraConfigParser m_parser;
    camera_manager::EmulatorCameraMng m_emulator_manager;
public:
    Foo() : m_emulator_manager(m_parser) {}
}
</code></pre>

